[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: learning.WHEN_TO_UPDATE
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[WHEN_TO_UPDATE]
overview: Criteria for when documentation should be updated
decision: Check each criterion. Update only if AT LEAST ONE matches.

[CRITERIA_1_USER_SAID_IT]
trigger: User explicitly states a rule, constraint, or principle
examples:
  - "Remember: never touch migrations without my approval"
  - "This is an architectural rule: no global state in the service layer"
  - "Constraint we discovered: use immutable DTOs across module boundaries"
action: UPDATE immediately (explicit knowledge from domain expert)
files: Typically CONSTRAINTS.toon or the most relevant domain file

[CRITERIA_2_FOUND_IN_CODE]
trigger: Discovery of architectural rule/pattern in source code
how_to_identify:
  - Comments with "MUST", "NEVER", "ALWAYS", "WARNING", "DO NOT"
  - Consistent patterns repeated across multiple files
  - Safety checks / asserts that reveal hidden constraints
  - Configuration constants that define hard limits
examples:
  - Found: // MUST rotate session keys every 30 days
  - Found: // NEVER reuse a (key, nonce) pair
  - Found: assert(buffer_size < 64 * 1024); // hard limit
action: UPDATE (verified from implementation)
files: CONSTRAINTS.toon, ARCHITECTURE.toon, or domain-specific file

[CRITERIA_3_DISCOVERED_THROUGH_WORK]
trigger: Understanding gained while implementing or debugging
when: You have conclusive evidence of how something works
examples:
  - "Now I understand: the cache layer uses weak references to break cycles"
  - "Discovered: the session pool reuses connections across requests"
  - "Verified: ownership of the loader is exclusive to the bootstrap module"
evidence_required:
  - Read the actual code confirming this
  - Understand WHY it works this way
  - Not a guess or pattern-match assumption
action: UPDATE (verified through code analysis)
files: ARCHITECTURE.toon or the relevant domain file

[CRITERIA_4_FIXING_ERROR]
trigger: Found inaccuracy or outdated info in existing docs
examples:
  - "CONSTRAINTS.toon says module X uses raw pointers, but it's actually smart pointers"
  - "PROJECT.toon says feature Y is in progress, but code shows it's complete"
  - "ARCHITECTURE.toon is missing a newly added layer"
action: UPDATE immediately (correctness matters)
files: Any file with the error

[CRITERIA_5_SIGNIFICANT_PATTERN]
trigger: Pattern appears in 3+ places and is not documented
how_to_verify:
  - Found in at least 3 different locations
  - Not in current documentation
  - Not an obvious standard practice
examples:
  - "All layer N→N+1 calls use a common error-handling wrapper"
  - "Every network operation validates the peer cert before use"
  - "All DTOs are frozen/immutable via a shared decorator"
action: UPDATE (prevents re-discovery in future)
files: Appropriate file for the pattern

[CRITERIA_6_STRUCTURE_CHANGED]
trigger: Project file/directory structure physically changes
how_to_verify:
  - New files/directories created
  - Existing files moved or reorganized
  - Module structure refactored
examples:
  - "Created new src/services/billing/ directory with 4 modules"
  - "Moved API handlers to src/api/v2/"
  - "Split monolith into src/core/ and src/plugins/"
action: UPDATE (keeps PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md current)
files: PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md (keep tree accurate)

[COMBINED_DECISION_TREE]
├─ User said it explicitly?                           → UPDATE
├─ Found warning/MUST/NEVER in code?                  → UPDATE
├─ Verified understanding from code analysis?         → UPDATE
├─ Found error in existing docs?                      → UPDATE
├─ Pattern appears in 3+ places undocumented?         → UPDATE
├─ Project file/directory structure physically changed? → UPDATE PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md
└─ None of the above?                                 → DON'T UPDATE
